    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38030?c=unm": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Research",
      "description": "Requisition: 38030 - Assistant Vice President for Research - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Vice President for Research Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38030 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Assistant Vice President for Research Posting Number req38030 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Research Hiring Department VP Resrch & Econ Devlpmnt VPRED (798A) Academic Location Vice President for Research Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR) invites applications for the position of Assistant Vice President for Research Infrastructure, reporting directly to the Vice President for Research (VPR) and will be an associate or full research professor determined by the individual's research background.  The Assistant Vice President for Research serves as senior advisor to the VPR regarding strategic development and stewardship of UNM’s research enterprise, including participating in strategic planning and management of OVPR Category 3 center and institute assets. The portfolio includes responsibility for the areas within the OVPR listed below.  This is a 12-month position, subject to review and renewal on an annual basis. The final FTE of the Assistant VPR role will be negotiated to accommodate candidates who choose to maintain an active research portfolio. Areas of responsibility for this position include: Research Facilities and Core Facilities (30%) Provide executive oversight for university research infrastructure, including shared instrumentation, core facilities, laboratories, and specialized research centers, including developing strategic plans for the growth, modernization, and sustainability of research facilities to support current and emerging research needs. Promote shared-resource models that maximize utilization, foster interdisciplinary research, and enhance competitiveness for external funding, including establishing policies (e.g., facilities use agreements), governance structures, and operational standards that promote excellence, accessibility, compliance, and efficient and effective utilization of research resources by both internal researchers and external partners. Collaborate with facility directors, faculty, and university leadership to prioritize investments in research equipment, technology, and infrastructure. Oversee the financial management and business operations of core facilities, including budgeting, cost recovery models, and long-term sustainability planning. Represent research infrastructure priorities in institutional planning efforts and advocate for investments that advance the university's research mission. National Laboratory and Industry User Facility and Shared Research Infrastructure Management (25%) Serve as the university's primary research facilities liaison to Los Alamos National Laboratory (LANL), Sandia National Laboratories (SNL), the Air Force Research Laboratory (AFRL), and other federal research laboratories to strengthen research-based strategic partnerships and collaborative initiatives. Promote coordination of research facilities at national laboratories, including user facilities (i.e. CINT, Quantum Demonstration Facility, and CAMINO), and UNM research facilities, including user facilities (i.e. CHTM, CMEM, and ARTsLab), to maximize research and training effectiveness and reduce duplication of regional resources Promote and coordinate utilization of UNM research facilities by private partners, including regional industry and start-ups to maximize utilization of facilities and their sustainability. Work with the OVPR’s Office of Research, Technology, Innovation, and Partnerships (ORTIP) to identify and advance opportunities to enhance the university’s role in addressing national and regional priorities through external partnerships (national labs, industry), faculty engagement with national laboratory research programs, user facilities, and funding initiatives, and trainee experiences, fellowships, and career pathways. Monitor federal research and laboratory initiatives to identify emerging opportunities that align with institutional strengths and strategic priorities and coordinate institutional participation in such initiatives as laboratory-sponsored research programs, educational initiatives, and regional innovation partnerships. Work with university and laboratory leadership to foster relationships that advance the university's research, education, and workforce development missions through agreements, frameworks, and strategic initiatives that expand collaborative research and innovation activities. Faculty, Postdoctoral Scholar, and Graduate Student Success Programs (40%) Provide strategic leadership, oversight, and assessment for faculty, staff, and student success initiatives and recognition (e.g., research awards) initiatives that support research excellence, including the WeR1 Faculty Success Program, the Zancada Graduate Fellowship Program, the Office of Postdoctoral Affairs (OPA), and the STEM-H Center (joint with HSC). Collaborate with the Faculty Research Development Office (FRDO), UNM ADVANCE, and Academic Affairs to develop and implement research-focused programs that enhance faculty research development, mentoring, scholarly productivity, external funding competitiveness, and engagement with UNM’s research infrastructure and partnerships. Lead initiatives that promote and expand undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral participation in research, experiential learning, and career development opportunities. Partner with academic leaders, faculty, and administrative units to align faculty and student success programs with institutional strategic priorities and serve as a resource regarding national laboratory partnerships for UNM researchers. Collaborate with the Faculty Research Development Office (FRDO) to identify and pursue external funding opportunities to sustain and expand faculty development, graduate student, and postdoctoral success programs. Leadership and Strategic Engagement (5%) Serve as an OVPR executive team member and senior advisor to the Vice President for Research on faculty success, student research engagement, national laboratory partnerships, and research infrastructure strategy. Work with the VPR and the AVP for External Relations to build and maintain partnerships with academic units, government agencies, industry partners, and community stakeholders to advance research and workforce development goals. Lead cross-functional teams and committees focused on enhancing the university's research ecosystem/infrastructure and institutional impact. Champion a culture of innovation, collaboration, inclusion, and operational excellence across faculty development, student success, and research support programs. Qualifications Minimum Job Requirements: Earned doctorate in a research-intensive field from an accredited institution. Minimum of 10 years of combined active research experience as principal investigator and/or in leadership or oversight roles supporting research operations at a large public or private academic/research institution Preferred Qualifications: Significant experience leading one or more aspects of research administration at a university or research institution Experience in establishing, running, and/or overseeing research facilities and core facilities Broad experience working across multiple sectors and/or disciplines to develop successful research-focused partnerships A record of successful collaboration with national laboratories, consortia, and/or industry partners in a research environment Commitment to effectively cultivating discovery, innovation and entrepreneurship among faculty, staff, and students Excellent and proven administrative and managerial skills, including leadership and team building, and strong interpersonal skills, including successful conflict resolution Established track record procuring external funding as appropriate to candidate’s field Excellent written communication, oral communication, and presentation skills across disciplines, sectors, and communities A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Completed applications must include a letter of interest describing qualifications for the position, current curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of at least three professional references. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/26/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38150?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 38150",
      "description": "Requisition: 38150 - Asst Prof-Secondary Ed Math and/or Science - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Asst Prof-Secondary Ed Math and/or Science Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38150 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Asst Prof-Secondary Ed Math and/or Science Posting Number req38150 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Tenure/Tenure-Track Hiring Department Dept Teacher Ed, Ed Lead & Policy (795A) Academic Location College of Education Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Teacher Education, Educational Leadership, and Policy (TEELP) invites applications for an Assistant Professor position to become part of the Secondary Education program and work with undergraduate and graduate students in TEELP. The candidate’s research and teaching experience will reflect preparation in secondary education Math and/or Science with a specialization in urban and/or rural and Indigenous settings as well as with Martinez/Yazzie student populations: Hispanic, Indigenous, Economically Disadvantaged, Multilingual, Special Needs. The successful candidate will have a completed Ph.D. or Ed.D. in math and/or science education, curriculum and instruction, and/or closely related fields by the starting date of the appointment. The successful candidate will have experience teaching math and/or science within secondary education (6-12) and working with the various student populations that represent New Mexico: Hispanic, Indigenous, Economically Disadvantaged, Multilingual, Special Needs . Experience with program development, particularly related to STEM secondary education, is also preferred. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: 1. Earned doctorate from an accredited university in MATH AND/OR SCIENCE Education, Curriculum and Instruction, or a closely related field. All requirements for the doctorate must be completed by the time of the start date of the appointment. 2. Minimum of three years of successful experience as a Secondary MATH AND/OR SCIENCE educator (6-12). 3. Evidence of research related to the position. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Minimum of five (5) years of experience teaching MATH AND/OR SCIENCE in public secondary (grades 6-12) schools in urban, rural, or high need districts. 2. Demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities. 3. Evidence of excellence or potential for excellence in teaching courses in Secondary MATH AND/OR SCIENCE education, MATH AND/OR SCIENCE methods, or related field. 4. Evidence of excellence or potential for excellence in conducting research in Secondary MATH AND/OR SCIENCE education. 5. Ability to propose and develop innovative courses and programs that support professional learning for teachers around MATH AND/OR SCIENCE that would also be embraced as relevant and timely for the Peoples of New Mexico. 6. Experience with or knowledge of MATH AND/OR SCIENCE education in urban and/or rural and Indigenous settings as well as with Yazzie/Martinez student populations for 5 plus years: Hispanic, Indigenous, Economically Disadvantaged, Multilingual, Special Needs. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. To apply, candidates should submit a complete application for review, including all of the following items. Only application materials requested will be considered:\n\n1.\tA signed letter of application (cover letter), including a statement of qualifications in relation to the Minimum and Preferred Qualifications criteria described below. Because the University is committed to serving the rich and varied cultures and communities of New Mexico, applicants should include information about how they will further this objective in their cover letter. Please limit the application letter to two pages.\n2.\tA statement of teaching where you discuss your teaching philosophy and how you prepare pre/in-service teachers who can successfully serve Martinez/Yazzie student populations: Hispanic, Indigenous, Economically Disadvantaged, Multilingual, Special Needs. Please limit the teaching statement to two pages.\n3.\tA statement of research where you discuss your research area and how you prepare pre/in-service teachers who can successfully serve Martinez/Yazzie student populations: Hispanic, Indigenous, Economically Disadvantaged, Multilingual, Special Needs. Please limit the teaching statement to two pages.\n4.\tA complete and up-to-date curriculum vitae (CV).\n5.\tTranscripts of all graduate coursework (from highest degree and content area; unofficial are acceptable for application submission, but official transcripts are required if selected for a campus interview).\n6.\tThe names, addresses, telephone numbers, and e-mail addresses of three professional references.\n7.\tA letter from the graduate chair indicating the status of dissertation work (required only for Doctoral Candidate applicants).\n\nOnly requested application materials will be considered. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 11/4/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38084?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 38084",
      "description": "Requisition: 38084 - Open Rank of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences- Adult Inpatient Attending - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open Rank of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences- Adult Inpatient Attending Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38084 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search Open Rank of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences- Adult Inpatient Attending Posting Number req38084 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Open Rank Hiring Department Psychiatry Psych (451A) Academic Location School of Medicine Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The UNM Department of Psychiatry and\nBehavioral Sciences is eager to put together the right package for an\nindividual with a passion for adult inpatient psychiatry and teaching, coupled\nwith an interest in joining a team of talented, caring and committed faculty\nmembers. Applications are being accepted for an academic faculty psychiatrist,\nsuitable for appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or full\nProfessor, for a position as an inpatient attending psychiatrist on our Adult Psychiatry\nDivision’s Inpatient Service . Clinical assignment will be at UNM Psychiatric\nCenter. The successful candidate can take full advantage of opportunities\navailable in our vibrant and active academic community. As an attending psychiatrist in our\n32-bed adult psychiatry inpatient service, the person selected will have a\nvoice in developing the unit’s direction as well as opportunities for\nmulticultural clinical care and scholarly and collaborative research activities\nacross the Health Sciences campus. There are many opportunities for\nprofessional development in leadership, administration, and education,\nincluding mentoring and supervision of medical students, residents, fellows,\nand trainees in related disciplines. Salary and academic rank are\ncommensurate with experience and academic background. Qualifications Minimum\nQualifications: Doctorate\nDegree (MD or equivalent); Board certified\nor board eligible in General Psychiatry; Clinical\nexperience – minimum 1 year; Licensable in\nNew Mexico; Must be\neligible to work in the United States. Preferred\nQualifications: Educational,\nteaching and supervision experience with residents, fellows and medical\nstudents; Clinical\nleadership experience in an academic setting; A demonstrated\ncommitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New\nMexico and to the success of the University's mission to serve local and global\ncommunities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. A complete application will include a cover letter addressing each of the minimum and preferred qualifications and describing the applicant’s accomplishments and future goals; a current CV; and the names, addresses and contact information for three professional references. A selection committee will invite the most promising applicants for interviews. For Additional Information Contact: Davin Quinn, MD, Professor and Vice Chair for Adult Clinical Services, DQuinn@salud.unm.edu For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/17/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
