    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38104?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 38104",
      "description": "Requisition: 38104 - Open Rank in Orthopaedics-Total Joint/Adult Reconstruction - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open Rank in Orthopaedics-Total Joint/Adult Reconstruction Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38104 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search Open Rank in Orthopaedics-Total Joint/Adult Reconstruction Posting Number req38104 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Flex Track Hiring Department Orthopaedics (497A) Academic Location School of Medicine Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Orthopaedics and Rehabilitation at the University of New Mexico School of Medicine is actively seeking a full-time faculty member who is fellowship trained in Total Joint/Adult Reconstruction.  The successful candidates will join other faculty in the Division of Total Joint/Adult Reconstruction in the Department. This academic appointment is in the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery and Rehabilitation. The position will be based at UNM Sandoval Regional Medical Center (SRMC) and the University of New Mexico Hospital (UNMH). Academic rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position provides a unique opportunity for rapid clinical practice growth, collaborative multidisciplinary clinical and translational research, and an active role in the orthopaedic residency training program. Applicants should possess excellent interpersonal, clinical and teaching skills, and should be board certified or eligible for certification and eligible for licensure in the state of New Mexico. The University of New Mexico Department of Orthopaedic Surgery is in the midst of a growth-oriented transformation, with the addition of the UNM Center of Excellence for Orthopaedic Surgery and Rehabilitation at the UNM SRMC campus. This 50,000 ft2 facility is home to state-of-the-art clinical, rehabilitation, research and academic spaces. We invite you to join our diverse, world-class faculty in providing the highest level of care to the people of New Mexico and the greater Mountain West region. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Candidate must hold an M.D. or D.O. degree, be Board Certified or Board Eligible with the American Board of Orthopaedic Surgery, completed residency in orthopaedic surgery, completed a fellowship in adult reconstruction surgery (total joints), hold or be eligible for medical license in state of New Mexico. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in teaching, experience in clinical care with both primary and revision total joint reconstruction, proven scholarly achievement, experience working with diverse populations, and a demonstrated commitment to resident and student success. A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global communities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Please provide:\n-Cover Letter addressing minimum and preferred qualifications.  \n-Current C.V.\n-3 Professional references/Letters of recommendation.\nPlease direct all inquiries to : Dr. Gehron Treme, Professor and  Chair c/o Michael Morris, Department Administrator.\nEmail: MiWMorris@salud.unm.edu Phone: (505) 272-4107 Address: MSC 10 5600, 1 University of New Mexico, Albuquerque, NM  87131 For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 12/14/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38046?c=unm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Anthropology",
      "description": "Requisition: 38046 - Assistant Professor-Anthropology - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor-Anthropology Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38046 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor-Anthropology Posting Number req38046 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Tenure/Tenure-Track Hiring Department Anthropology Department (045A) Academic Location College of Arts & Sciences Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The UNM Department of Anthropology invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor of Archaeology to begin in August 2027. We seek to hire an integrative archaeologist with a focus in the analysis of stable isotopes to address anthropological questions, including but not limited to the reconstruction past human habitats, diets, modifications of the environment, or responses to climate change. Research foci should complement, and not duplicate, existing specializations in our program. UNM Archaeology has long been a leader in theoretically informed, question-driven, and methodologically sophisticated anthropological archaeological research addressing long-term perspectives on the human experience across the globe. The successful candidate will add to Archaeology’s record of innovative, collaborative, and ground-breaking research on cultural dynamics and past human-environment interactions. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to become a core faculty member in the UNM Center for Stable Isotopes (CSI), an interdisciplinary research and analytical facility supporting stable isotope research across Anthropology, Biology, Earth and Planetary Sciences, Chemistry, and the Biomedical Sciences. The candidate will collaborate with faculty and students across these disciplines and help train early career scientists in stable isotope methods. The position offers opportunities to expand CSI’s state-of-the-art analytical capacity through the development of new methods and capabilities. We seek a scientist who thrives in the laboratory and is committed to instrument development, calibration, quality control, operation, maintenance, and troubleshooting. The successful candidate will also have opportunities to contribute to our two-week summer training course, IsoCamp (isocamp.org), and to pursue a leadership role within CSI. CSI is a student-centered facility that provides broad access to instrumentation as well as hands-on training opportunities. The existing user community at CSI provides a strong foundation for building an internationally visible research program and offers experiential training opportunities for graduate and undergraduate students, which will enhance the successful candidate’s potential for developing collaborations across UNM and beyond. Learn more about our program: https://anthropology.unm.edu/research/areas/index.html Learn more about the Center for Stable Isotopes: csi.unm.edu Complete applications must include · Letter of intent explaining the applicant’s minimum and preferred qualifications for the position · A research statement, including a five-year research plan (max 3 pages) · A statement on teaching philosophy, interests, and experience (max 3 pages) · Curriculum vitae · Full contact information for three references To apply, please access the University of New Mexico’s online application system at https://www.unmedu/jobs and apply for posting requisition #38046. Only applications submitted through this website can be considered. Applicants should pay extra attention to the “Special Instructions to Applicants,” which detail all of the required elements that must accompany the application. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For best consideration, all required application materials must be received by November 8, 2026. We will only consider complete applications. The position will remain open until filled. Inquiries about the position should be directed to the search committee chair (Hannah Mattson, hmattson@unm.edu). Inquiries about the online application process can be directed to the Search coordinator, Jennifer George (jgeorge2@unm.edu). The University of New Mexico is an EEO/AA Employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. UNM is the premier research university in New Mexico, is a Carnegie Highest Research Activity Institution.  Our campus is located in the heart of Albuquerque, which has cultural, outdoor and recreational opportunities for everyone.  Learn more about our city, our welcoming campus, and research opportunities at http://advance.unm.edu/why-abq/ and  https://advance.unm.edu/why-unm/.  For more information regarding the College of Arts and Science's ambitious hiring plan, including a list of departments that are hiring faculty members with shared interests, please see this page Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: · PhD in Anthropology or Archaeology, conferred at time of application · An active laboratory research program · Expertise in stable isotope analysis · Ability to teach introductory level classes in archaeology Preferred Qualifications: · Evidence of research quality, productivity, and impact as demonstrated by a record of publications and other recognition appropriate to career stage · Evidence of the potential to develop a vigorous externally funded research program · Potential to collaborate in integrative interdisciplinary research that complements, but does not duplicate, existing strengths in the department and at UNM · Demonstrated teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels · Ability to teach courses in the archaeology of a geographic region, a major theoretical topic, or area of expertise · Demonstrated experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students · Ability to develop new courses that would take advantage of CSI’s analytical capabilities and an interest in advancing the scientific and educational mission of CSI through contributions to its analytical capabilities, hands-on training activities, and collaborative shared-use laboratory environment. · A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the university’s mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Complete applications must include\n•\tLetter of intent explaining the applicant’s minimum and preferred qualifications for the position\n•\tA research statement, including a five-year research plan (max 3 pages)\n•\tA statement on teaching philosophy, interests, and experience (max 3 pages)\n•\tCurriculum vitae \n•\tFull contact information for three references Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 11/8/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-