    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38109?c=unm": {
      "title": "Lecturer II",
      "description": "Requisition: 38109 - Lecturer II - Project Management - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lecturer II - Project Management Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38109 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/29/2026 Back to Search Lecturer II - Project Management Posting Number req38109 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Lecturer Hiring Department ASM FI Department Administration (039D) Academic Location Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Finance and Innovation within the Ellis School of Business Leadership (formerly Anderson School of Management) at the University of New Mexico is seeking qualified candidates for a Lecturer II position in Project Management to begin August 2027. This is a teaching-focused faculty position with primary responsibility for high-quality instruction in Project Management at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will normally teach a 4/4 course load and will be expected to contribute to the continued development of the Project Management curriculum and student experience. Research is not an expectation of the position. The James & Gail Ellis School of Business Leadership (Ellis) is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) International and is one of the few in the world to attain both an Accounting and Business Accreditation from AACSB. We offer BBA and MBA degrees in eight active concentrations as well as an Executive MBA for working professionals. With over 27,000 alumni, Ellis alums can be found having an impact in their communities all over the world. Ellis emphasizes collaborative student interaction, active adult learning, team experiences, and scholarship that draw upon a variety of methodologies and subject areas. New Mexico represents a wide range of perspectives with a rich cultural heritage. The richness of our community is demonstrated both internally ( http://www.unm.edu/welcome/ ) and within the city ( https://advance.unm.edu/why-abq/ ) and state ( https://www.newmexico.org/ ). The University of New Mexico seeks highly qualified faculty who can contribute to the University's mission and values and continue to build the excellent research and teaching climate of Ellis School of Business Leadership. The Finance and Innovation faculty supports existing BBA and MBA programs, including concentrations in Project Management. Teaching responsibilities for this position include undergraduate and graduate courses in Project Management. The Finance and Innovation group is a small, cohesive group seeking colleagues who demonstrate a willingness to make a commitment to maintaining and building a strong Project Management area within the Ellis School of Business Leadership. For information about the Ellis School of Business Leadership and the Department of Finance and Innovation faculty, see https://business.unm.edu/ . Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess a Master’s degree in Business, Engineering, or a closely related field by the application date Record of Teaching Experience within the last five (5) years Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of professional, scholarly, or applied activities that support teaching and curriculum development in Project Management Evidence of excellence or promise of achieving excellence in teaching Project Management courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels Has designated faculty qualifications that meet one of the four AACSB accredited categories: Scholarly Academic (SA), Practice Academic (PA), Scholarly Practitioner (SP), and Instructional Practitioner (IP) A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Each applicant will be instructed to provide: A cover letter of application, including a statement of qualifications in relation to the Minimum and Preferred Qualifications, A complete and up-to-date curriculum vita, Teaching/mentoring statement, Letters of Recommendation, if available, Transcripts of all graduate coursework (readable, unofficial copies will be accepted), The names and contact information of three to five professional references, Teaching/Course Evaluations and/or corresponding syllabi, A sample of one professional work product, publication, and/or presentation relevant toproject management. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/30/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38119?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 38119",
      "description": "Requisition: 38119 - Temp Part-Time Faculty in Human Services - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temp Part-Time Faculty in Human Services Gallup, NM, United States | req38119 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Temp Part-Time Faculty in Human Services Posting Number req38119 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Adjunct Hiring Department Gallup Branch Academic Location Gallup Branch Campus Gallup Benefits Eligible Adjunct faculty may be eligible to receive certain UNM benefits in some cases. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary PLEASE NOTE: This position is for the\n  UNM-Gallup Branch, located in Gallup, NM, approximately 138 miles west of\n  Albuquerque, NM. The University of New\n  Mexico Gallup Branch Nursing and Human Services Division, anticipates hiring\n  adjunct faculty to teach face-to-face and/or online lower division courses\n  (1000/2000 Level) in the Spring, Summer, and Fall 2027 semesters in the\n  following potential disciplines: Possible Courses: HMSV 1120 -   Interviewing Techniques HMSV 2215 -   Adolescence Substance Abuse: Prevention and Treatment HMSV 2270 - Substance   Abuse in Families HMSV 2320 -   Professional Issues in Human Services HMSV 2998 - Substance   Abuse Counseling Field Experience HMSV 2230 - Alcohol   and Substance Abuse Counseling SOWK 2110 -   Introduction to Human Services and Social Work HCHS 140 -   Introduction to Substance Abuse HMSV 1110 - Group   Dynamics FCST 1120 -   Introduction to Family and Child Studies FCST 2130 - Marriage   and Family Relationships The\n  University of New Mexico established branch colleges to provide the highest\n  quality of education for students pursuing post-secondary education at\n  different locations throughout the state. Branch colleges respond\n  specifically to the unique needs and multicultural backgrounds of their\n  respective communities by offering community education programs, career and\n  technical education including certificate and associate degree programs, and\n  transfer programs that prepare students for upper division entry into\n  colleges and universities. The Nursing and Human Services Division at UNM Gallup Branch is seeking a\n  qualified temporary part-time faculty member to teach lower division classes\n  in various courses or topics as specified above. UNM Gallup instructors are\n  responsible for all aspects of any class they are teaching including but not\n  limited to meeting face-to-face with the class during assigned times that may\n  include evenings or weekends, content delivery, assignment development,\n  grading assignments, reporting of grades, and assessment of student learning\n  as outlined by the division chair. Positions are contingent upon need each semester as determined by\n  departmental needs, student enrollment levels, current course offering\n  matrix, and demand driven by graduation requirements.  Positions may be filled or eliminated each\n  semester up to the deadline for students to drop or add courses.  Candidates selected for these positions\n  will report to the NHS Division Chair. Wages: Adjunct Faculty are currently compensated on the basis of their credentials\n  and credit hour course loads. Best Consideration Dates: For best consideration please apply by these dates: October 08, 2026 for Spring 2027 Semester January 15, 2027 for Summer & Fall 2027 Semester Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Master's Degree in Social Work, Human Services or related field; or a Master’s degree and 18 graduate hours in any of those fields previously listed. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate degree in Social Work, Human Services or related field One or more years college or adult teaching experience at a branch/community college or similar institution Clinical experiences in the area of expertise such as child welfare, mental health, public health, diabetes prevention or domestic violence etc. Clinical experience in area of substance abuse Has a license through the NM Counseling and Therapy Practice Board Demonstrated ability to work in groups in a collaborative atmosphere A demonstrated commitment\nto cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied culture of New Mexico and\nto the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Please attach the following materials to your online application: 1.) An updated curriculum vitae; 2.) Transcript(s) sufficient to assess minimum qualifications; 3.) Cover letter indicating which discipline(s) you are interested in teaching, the days/times you are available to teach, and how your education satisfies the minimum qualifications criteria; and 4.) Three professional references who can speak to your directly relevant knowledge, skills, and experience.  Please include both phone number and email addresses. Each of these MUST be uploaded for applicant consideration. When submitting your application materials, please ensure all attachments are provided in PDF format for optimal viewing and processing. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration This posting will remain active until . Anyone who applies for a position under this posting will automatically be considered for openings in subsequent semesters unless they indicate in their cover letter that they are not interested in teaching in specific semesters. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38116?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 38116",
      "description": "Requisition: 38116 - Temp Part-Time Faculty in Physical Education (PE) - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temp Part-Time Faculty in Physical Education (PE) Gallup, NM, United States | req38116 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Temp Part-Time Faculty in Physical Education (PE) Posting Number req38116 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Adjunct Hiring Department Gallup Branch Academic Location Gallup Branch Campus Gallup Benefits Eligible Adjunct faculty may be eligible to receive certain UNM benefits in some cases. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary This position is for the University\nof New Mexico-Gallup Branch located in Gallup, NM, approximately 138 miles west\nof Albuquerque, NM The University of New Mexico Gallup\nBranch, Liberal Arts & Education Division seeks to hire temporary part-time\nfaculty members to teach face-to-face undergraduate-level physical activity,\nexercise and/or wellness-related classes in the Spring, Summer and Fall 2027 semesters. Some of these courses include: Possible Courses - PHED 1110 – Dance - PHED 1140 – Zumba - PHED 1210 – Basketball - PHED 1230 – Individual Sport\n(varies) - PHED 1280 – Volleyball - PHED 1290 – Team Sport (varies) - PHED 1310 – Swim I - PHED 1410 – Yoga - PHED 1420 – Stretch and Relax - PHED 1430 – Pilates - PHED 1440 – Tai Chi - PHED 1460 – Conditioning - PHED 1510 – Training - PHED 1620 – Fitness - PHED 1670 – Aerobics - PHED 1710 – Martial Arts - PHED 1830 – Running - PHED 1910 – Outdoor Experience - PHED 1996 – Topics (varies) Candidates should indicate on their cover letter the area, or\nareas, of their interest, expertise, and experience. Candidates\nmay also indicate potential new courses in their cover letter should their\neducation and credential provide sufficient support. UNM Gallup instructors are responsible for all aspects of any\nclass they are teaching including but not limited to meeting with the class\nduring assigned times that may include online, evenings and/or weekends,\ncontent delivery, assignment development, grading assignments, reporting of\ngrades, and assessment of student learning as outlined by the department chair. Positions are contingent upon need each semester as determined by student\nenrollment levels, current course offering matrix, and demand driven by\ngraduation requirements.  Positions may be filled or eliminated each\nsemester up to the deadline for students to drop or add courses.\n Candidates who are selected for these positions will report to the\ndivision chair. Salary Adjunct faculty are currently compensated on the\nbasis of their credentials and credit hour course loads. Salary range:\n$1,157.97 - $1,240.52 per credit hour. Best Consideration Dates For best consideration please apply by these dates: November 15, 2026 Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Extensive\nknowledge, skills, and abilities in area of expertise, along with leadership,\ncommunication, and organizational skills Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s\ndegree in kinesiology, exercise science, fitness management, or related degree Appropriate activity certification, as needed (see application instructions) American Red Cross CPR/Basic Life Support certification (can also be earned\nwithin 30 days of employment) Teaching experience preferred A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Only applications submitted through the official UNMJobs site will be accepted.\nCover letter and resume are also required. In the cover letter, the applicant should explain how their resume and work history satisfies any and all of the Higher Learning Commission credentialing factors for the Physical Education Non-Professional activity courses they are applying to instruct. These factors may include: 1. An Associate or Baccalaureate degree in physical education or related field; 2. Certification and/or advanced achievement in the content area and/or as a health fitness instructor from a credible national organization, board or accrediting body; 3. Professional performance, honors, awards, or significant recognition that indicates the individual’s level of discipline-based content knowledge; or 4. Other demonstrated competencies and achievements relevant to the content of the course. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration This posting will remain active until 11/15/2026. Anyone who applies for a position under this posting will automatically be considered for openings in subsequent semesters unless they indicate in their cover letter that they are not interested in teaching in specific semesters. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38114?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 38114",
      "description": "Requisition: 38114 - Chief Medical Investigator - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Chief Medical Investigator Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38114 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Chief Medical Investigator Posting Number req38114 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Open Rank Hiring Department SOM Faculty Affairs (117A) Academic Location School of Medicine Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The University\nof New Mexico, School of Medicine located in Albuquerque, NM at the Health\nSciences Center is seeking a dynamic leader to serve as Chief Medical\nInvestigator at the New Mexico Office of the Medical Investigator (OMI) . The Chief is\nselected by the Board of Medical Investigations. The Chief reports to the Board\nfor OMI affairs via the Dean of the School of Medicine and the Chair of\nPathology for academic activities. The Chief also\nmust work collaboratively with the faculty from the UNM School of Medicine, law\nenforcement officers, officers of the court, funeral directors, and\nrepresentatives of the Department of Health. The Chief\nMedical Investigator of the OMI will serve as the key leader and advocate in\nall matters concerning clinical service, education, and research related to the\npractice of forensic pathology. This includes overseeing all administrative\nmatters including the management of short- and long-range planning, staffing,\nbudgeting, scheduling, and accreditation. The responsibilities also include\nperforming postmortem examinations and providing testimony in criminal and\ncivil courts. For court testimony in remote counties, transportation is\nprovided by a private charter air transportation service. The Chief plans\nand manages the total operations of the OMI, develops and implements office\nobjectives and long-range plans, and will be aware of the emerging scientific,\npolitical, and funding trends on all levels. Educational responsibilities\ninclude the supervision and instruction of forensic pathology fellows,\npathology residents, medical students, medical investigators and others. The OMI is\nunique among medical examiner offices in that it is a statewide agency in which\nthe forensic pathologists have full-time faculty appointments within the\nUniversity of New Mexico School of Medicine Department of Pathology. The NM Office\nof the Medical Investigator is in the high desert community of Albuquerque, New\nMexico. Abundant recreational opportunities exist within our diverse and\nculturally rich city. Albuquerque enjoys a temperate climate with 310 days of\nsunshine as well as four distinct seasons. Salary is negotiable depending upon\nqualifications and experience. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: the\nChief Medical Investigator must hold an MD/DO or equivalent degree; be\ncertified by the American Board of Pathology in anatomic and forensic pathology;\nbe qualified for an appointment as an Associate Professor or Professor in the\nUNM Department of Pathology; possess at least 6 years of experience in the\nclinical practice of forensic pathology; and have at least 3 years demonstrated\nexperience in leadership roles at an operational level within a medical\nexaminer’s office. Preferred\nQualifications: Administration: Leadership and\npractical skills in management include fiscal and budgetary experience and\ntraining in these areas Strong\ninterpersonal skills including experience with successful management of\nconflict resolution, consistent clear communication, respect for colleagues,\nand high expectations of excellence from faculty and staff Successful\nmentoring of faculty and staff Experience\nworking with legislative, executive, judicial, and law enforcement bodies as\nwell as the public at large and the media Ability to\naddress the specific concerns of New Mexico Hispanic and Native American\npopulations regarding the death investigation process, autopsies and their\nimpact on communities and families Education: Successful\ndevelopment and participation in educational programs Demonstrated\nsuccess in mentoring of trainees and faculty including forensic pathology\nfellows and pathology residents Research: Evidence of\nscholarly activity in the forensic sciences Evidence of\npursuit of grant funding Experience in\nmultidisciplinary research Service: Experienced\nleadership in medical examiner office operation Experience in\nobtaining or maintaining accreditation through the National Association of\nMedical Examiners (NAME) Practices\nclinical forensic pathology, in addition to administrative duties, in\naccordance with general practice guidelines of the office. Additional\nboard certification or training in areas such as: Neuropathology, Cardiac\npathology, Pediatric\npathology, Public health A demonstrated\ncommitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New\nMexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global\ncommunities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Nomination Process- to nominate an outstanding candidate please send the name and contact information of the nominee to: Chief Medical Investigator c/o April Rodriguez-Esparza; (505) 272-9767; amrodriguez@salud.unm.edu . Nominations must be received by October 6, 2026. If self-nominating, you need only apply and not submit a self-nomination. How to Apply- a complete application consists of (1) current curriculum vitae; (2) a comprehensive letter of interest that addresses how their strengths and experience match the qualifications for the position, and what they see as challenges and opportunities of the position in the current academic environment, and; (3) names, addresses and contact information for five references. Candidates will be consulted before references are contacted. All communications and questions regarding this position by interested applicants must be only made to April Rodriguez-Esparza, search coordinator or Dr. Justin Baca, Chair of the Search Committee. Mrs. Rodriguez-Esparza and Dr. Baca will place interested applicants in touch with relevant Pathology and OMI faculty to discuss the OMI’s programs and the position. This position may be subject to criminal records screening in accordance with New Mexico law. If criminal records screening is mandated, clearance by the New Mexico Department of Health is required as a condition of employment. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/15/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38102?c=unm": {
      "title": "Lecturer II",
      "description": "Requisition: 38102 - Lecturer II - Management Information Systems - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lecturer II - Management Information Systems Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38102 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Lecturer II - Management Information Systems Posting Number req38102 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Lecturer Hiring Department ASM Mrkting Info Decision Sci MIDS (039E) Academic Location Anderson School of Management Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Marketing, Information Systems, and Decision Sciences (MIDS) within the Ellis School of Business Leadership (formerly Anderson School of Management) at the University of New Mexico is seeking qualified candidates for a Lecturer II position in Management Information Systems (preferably Cybersecurity), with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The James & Gail Ellis School of Business Leadership (Ellis) is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) International and is one of the few in the world to attain both an Accounting and Business Accreditation from AACSB. We offer BBA and MBA degrees in eight active concentrations as well as an Executive MBA for working professionals. With over 27,000 alumni, Ellis alums can be found having an impact in their communities all over the world. Ellis emphasizes collaborative student interaction, active adult learning, team experiences, and scholarship that draw upon a variety of methodologies and subject areas. New Mexico represents a wide range of perspectives with a rich cultural heritage. The richness of our community is demonstrated both internally ( http://www.unm.edu/welcome/ ) and within the city ( https://advance.unm.edu/why-abq/ ) and state ( https://www.newmexico.org/ ). The University of New Mexico seeks highly qualified faculty who can contribute to the University's mission and values and continue to build the excellent research and teaching climate of Ellis School of Business Leadership. The MIDS Department faculty supports existing BBA and MBA programs, including concentrations in MIS, and an MS in Cybersecurity and Business Analytics. Teaching responsibilities for this position include undergraduate and graduate courses in Management Information Systems (preferably in Cybersecurity). The Marketing, Information Systems, and Decision Sciences group is a small, cohesive group seeking colleagues who demonstrate a willingness to make a commitment to maintaining and building a strong MIS area within the Ellis School of Business Leadership. For information about the Ellis School of Business Leadership and the Marketing, Information Systems, and Decision Sciences faculty, see https://business.unm.edu/ . Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess an earned master’s degree or have a strong prospect for completing a master’s degree in Management Information Systems, Information Systems, Cybersecurity or a closely related field from an accredited institution by August 2027. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of excellence or promise of achieving excellence in teaching MIS core and elective courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with emphasis on cybersecurity. Demonstrated ability or interest in teaching MIS core and elective courses, such as Cybersecurity, Databases, Programming, Network & Systems Administration, and Systems Analysis & Design, as well as other core/elective MIS courses as needed. Demonstrated ability or interest in teaching online. Familiarity with cybersecurity and risk-management frameworks (desirable for instructional currency). Has designated faculty qualifications that meet one of the four AACSB accredited categories: Scholarly Academic (SA), Practice Academic (PA), Scholarly Practitioner (SP), and Instructional Practitioner (IP) A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Each applicant will be instructed to provide: A cover letter indicating the candidate’s interests, goals, and qualifications for the position, elaborating on the preferred qualifications. A complete and up-to-date curriculum vita. Teaching statement. Transcripts of all graduate coursework (readable, unofficial copies will be accepted). Names and contact information of three professional references. Syllabi of course(s) taught (and sample instructional materials). Aggregate summaries of instructor evaluations or other evidence of excellence in teaching. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/29/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/38095?c=unm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Requisition: 38095 - Assistant Professor - Management Information Systems - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor - Management Information Systems Albuquerque, NM, United States | req38095 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor - Management Information Systems Posting Number req38095 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Tenure/Tenure-Track Hiring Department ASM Mrkting Info Decision Sci MIDS (039E) Academic Location Anderson School of Management Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Marketing, Information Systems, and Decision Sciences (MIDS) within the Ellis School of Business Leadership (formerly Anderson School of Management) at the University of New Mexico is seeking qualified candidates for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Management Information Systems (preferably in Cybersecurity), with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The James & Gail Ellis School of Business Leadership (Ellis) is accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB) International and is one of the few in the world to attain both an Accounting and Business Accreditation from AACSB. We offer BBA and MBA degrees in eight active concentrations as well as an Executive MBA for working professionals. With over 27,000 alumni, Ellis alums can be found having an impact in their communities all over the world. Ellis emphasizes collaborative student interaction, active adult learning, team experiences, and scholarship that draw upon a variety of methodologies and subject areas. New Mexico represents a wide range of perspectives with a rich cultural heritage. The richness of our community is demonstrated both internally ( http://www.unm.edu/welcome/ ) and within the city ( https://advance.unm.edu/why-abq/ ) and state ( https://www.newmexico.org/ ). The University of New Mexico seeks highly qualified faculty who can contribute to the University's mission and values and continue to build the excellent research and teaching climate of Ellis School of Business Leadership. The MIDS Department faculty supports existing BBA and MBA programs, including concentrations in MIS, and an MS in Cybersecurity and Business Analytics. Teaching responsibilities for this position include undergraduate and graduate courses in Management Information Systems (preferably in Cybersecurity). The Marketing, Information Systems, and Decision Sciences group is a small, cohesive group seeking colleagues who demonstrate a willingness to make a commitment to maintaining and building a strong MIS area within the Ellis School of Business Leadership. For information about the Ellis School of Business Leadership and the Marketing, Information Systems, and Decision Sciences faculty, see www.business.unm.edu . Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess an earned doctorate or have a strong prospect for completing a doctorate in Management Information Systems, Information Systems, Cybersecurity or a closely related field from an accredited institution by August 2027. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of or promise of a significant program of research and scholarship in cybersecurity and/or Management Information Systems Evidence of excellence or promise of achieving excellence in teaching MIS core and elective courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, with emphasis on cybersecurity. Demonstrated ability or interest in teaching MIS core and elective courses, such as Cybersecurity, Databases, Programming, Network & Systems Administration, and Systems Analysis & Design, as well as other core/elective MIS courses as needed. Demonstrated ability or interest in teaching online. A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Each applicant will be instructed to provide: A cover letter indicating the candidate’s interests, goals, and qualifications for the position, elaborating on the preferred qualifications. Applicants who have not yet defended their PhD dissertation will be asked to include an anticipated timeline for completion of their PhD. A complete and up-to-date curriculum vita. Research statement. Teaching statement. Transcripts of all graduate coursework (readable, unofficial copies will be accepted). Names and contact information of three to five professional references. Sample articles/publications. Syllabi of course(s) taught (and sample instructional materials). Aggregate summaries of instructor evaluations or other evidence of excellence in teaching. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/29/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
