    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37886?c=unm": {
      "title": "Comparative Animal Physiology - Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Requisition: 37886 - Comparative Animal Physiology - Assistant Professor of Biology - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Comparative Animal Physiology - Assistant Professor of Biology Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37886 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Comparative Animal Physiology - Assistant Professor of Biology Posting Number req37886 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Tenure/Tenure-Track Hiring Department Biology Department (048A) Academic Location College of Arts & Sciences Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Biology at the University of New Mexico invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Comparative Animal Physiology to begin in August 2027. Applicants must have a PhD in biology or a related field by date of application. For best consideration, all application materials must be received by November 6, 2026. Applications must demonstrate 1) the ability to develop a vigorous externally funded research program in comparative animal physiology including a lab and/or field component, 2) a promising publication record, 3) the ability to achieve excellence in teaching and mentoring, and 4) an interest in collaborating with faculty and students across a diverse array of fields. The new faculty member will be expected to teach a core undergraduate class in animal physiology, upper-level undergraduate and graduate courses related to their research interests, as well as to mentor masters and doctoral students. The Department of Biology at UNM is a broad unified department representing all fields of biology. It includes the Museum of Southwestern Biology (MSB), Center for Evolutionary and Theoretical Immunology (CETI), the Sevilleta Long-Term Ecological Research Program (SEV-LTER), Center for Stable Isotopes (CSI), and an Animal Research Facility that supports experimental work on terrestrial and aquatic model organisms.  The department has 35 tenure and tenure-track faculty as well as 11 lecturers, supports an active graduate program with >100 students, and has one of the most dynamic and successful research programs on campus. Qualifications Minimum and Preferred Criteria: Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Biology or closely related field by start date of application. At least one year of relevant postdoctoral experience by date of appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of strength or potential for excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, including the ability to teach undergraduate animal physiology Demonstrated potential for scholarship and impactful contributions to peer-reviewed literature Commitment to mentoring undergraduate and graduate students Potential to collaborate with faculty and students across diverse fields Evidence of potential to develop a vigorous, externally funded, research program A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global communities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. A complete application consists of 1) a cover letter describing the applicant’s qualifications as they relate to the minimum and preferred qualifications (2 pages or less), 2) a current curriculum vita, 3) a teaching statement (2 pages or less), 4) a statement of past and future research interests (3 pages or less), and 5) the names and contact information for 3 professional references. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 11/6/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
