    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37930?c=unm": {
      "title": "Lecturer I or II in Trades",
      "description": "Requisition: 37930 - Lecturer I or II in Trades at UNM-Valencia - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Lecturer I or II in Trades at UNM-Valencia Los Lunas, NM, United States | req37930 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/25/2026 Back to Search Lecturer I or II in Trades at UNM-Valencia Posting Number req37930 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Lecturer Hiring Department Valencia Branch Academic Location Valencia Branch Campus Valencia Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Business & Industrial\nTechnologies Division at UNM-Valencia Campus is accepting applications for a Lecturer I or II in the Trades, to include but not limited to welding,\nconstruction, plumbing, HVACR and electrical. This posting is for a full-time,\n9-month, non-tenure-track faculty position. The position begins January 11,\n2027. Located about 30 miles south of\nAlbuquerque in rural Valencia County, the University of New Mexico-Valencia\nCampus is a two-year branch community college associated with the University of\nNew Mexico. With an emphasis on teaching excellence, Valencia Campus offers\nvocational and technical courses as well as academic transfer courses to the\ncitizens of Valencia and northern Socorro counties. The faculty and staff serve\na student body of approximately 2,000 each semester. Salary: Base salary for this nine-month faculty position is\n$63,000. Summer teaching may be available\nbased on program needs, with additional compensation. Office space, computer\nhardware and software will be provided, as well as an excellent package of\nbenefits. Summary of\nduties and responsibilities: Duties include providing classroom and hands-on laboratory\ninstruction in trades-related courses offered through the Business &\nIndustrial Technologies Division. This includes but is not limited to preparing\ncourse materials, supervising laboratory activities, maintaining a safe and\norganized learning environment, assessing student performance, and maintaining\nattendance, scholastic, and student records. Responsibilities also include\nposting and maintaining office hours, participating in curriculum development\nand outcomes assessment, professional development related to the teaching\nfield, college committees, departmental projects, community and industry\npartnerships, and other duties as assigned. The position may include daytime\nand/or evening instruction at UNM-Valencia facilities and partner locations. If selected for an on-campus\ninterview, applicants may be asked to provide a teaching demonstration related\nto their trade area and documentation of professional experience, licenses,\ncertifications, or credentials. We will offer reimbursement for travel expenses to all candidates who\nare invited to UNM Valencia campus, who accept the offer of an interview, and\nwho must incur long-distance travel expenses. The reimbursement for travel will\nfollow UNM policy and will be no more than $1,000. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Degree in a career field or industry credentials in a career technical field or ten years of tested experience in an industry or technical field (as per Higher Learning Commission tested experience guidelines) Preferred Qualifications: Associate or bachelor’s degree in a career technical field Teaching experience in a career technical field Experience working with business and industry partners Experience across multiple trade areas or ability to teach more than one program area. A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global communities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/23/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37871?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 37871",
      "description": "Requisition: 37871 - Open Rank of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open Rank of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37871 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search Open Rank of Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine Posting Number req37871 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Clinician Educator Hiring Department Anesthesiology Faculty (772B) Academic Location School of Medicine Campus Health Sciences Center (HSC) - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department\nof Anesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine at the University of New Mexico in\nAlbuquerque, New Mexico, invites applications for a full-time faculty position\nat the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. The\nprimary appointment will be in the Department of Anesthesiology & Critical\nCare Medicine with clinical responsibilities in the Main Operating Room .\nSuccessful candidates will join a collaborative group of experienced\nanesthesiologists committed to excellence in patient care, education, research,\nand service. UNM Hospital is\nthe only Level I Trauma Center in New Mexico. Our Critical Care facilities\ninclude 192 beds, with 96 dedicated ICU beds, a 20-bed pediatric intensive care\nunit, 24-bed neonatal intensive care unit, 18-bed trauma surgical intensive\ncare unit, 6-bed burn center, and 24-bed neurosurgical intensive care unit. The successful\ncandidate will provide high-quality anesthesiology care, participate in the\neducation and mentorship of learners, and contribute to departmental academic\nand service initiatives. The University of New Mexico and the Department of\nAnesthesiology and Critical Care Medicine are committed to fostering a diverse,\ninclusive, and collaborative environment that supports our faculty, trainees,\npatients, and the communities we serve. Albuquerque, New\nMexico, offers more than 300+ days of sunshine annually and provides\nexceptional opportunities for outdoor activities, including hiking, climbing,\nskiing, and exploring more than 400 miles of local trails. Qualifications Minimum\nQualifications: Must hold\nunrestricted medical license Must hold M.D.\nor equivalent Must be Board\nCertified by the American Board of Anesthesiology or within three years of\nresidency and active in the certification process Preferred\nQualifications Resident\nTeaching Experience Research and\nScholarly Activities Must have\nrecent and active experience taking call in level 1 or level 3 trauma centers. A demonstrated\ncommitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New\nMexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global\ncommunities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Applicants should submit a CV and Cover Letter. The cover letter must address reasons for interest in the position and how experience meets the preferred qualifications for this position.  Please direct questions about the position to Dr. Christopher Arndt, CArndt@salud.unm.edu . Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 10/9/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter 