    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37804?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 37804",
      "description": "Requisition: 37804 - Open Rank of Family and Community Medicine - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open Rank of Family and Community Medicine Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37804 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/9/2026 Back to Search Open Rank of Family and Community Medicine Posting Number req37804 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Clinician Educator Hiring Department Family Community Medicine FCM (160B) Academic Location School of Medicine Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary Open Rank - Clinician Educator – Surgical FM/OB Physician The Department of Family and Community Medicine is seeking a Family Medicine physician with fellowship training in surgical obstetrics to join our faculty. The ideal candidate has a demonstrated commitment to service, education, and perinatal addiction care. This faculty role centers on Maternal Child Health and primary care within a mission‑driven, community‑focused department. The successful candidate will serve as an attending physician on the Family Medicine Maternal and Child Health (MCH) service, provide inpatient addiction consultation for pregnant patients with substance use disorders, have an outpatient primary care panel, and participate in newborn care at the University Hospital’s level I nursery, with potential involvement in the level II intermediate care nursery. Teaching is a core component of this position, including supervision and instruction of Family Medicine residents, MCH fellows, UNM medical students, and residents in Pediatrics and Obstetrics & Gynecology. Our MCH program is deeply rooted in community-based care, with established partnerships supporting rural family medicine practices, offering a rich environment for collaborative clinical care and training . Robust research opportunities are also available for faculty interested in scholarly work. Our Vision and Mission: Innovation, Partnership, Education, Research Our vision is that the well-being and healthcare of individuals, families and communities in New Mexico will be enhanced through our integration of and advocacy for the principles of Public Health and Family and Community Medicine. It is our mission to be leaders in partnering with communities to enhance the health and well-being of the people of New Mexico through innovative education, research and service. What We Are Known For Passionate about supporting and defining diversity, equity and inclusion towards improving the health of all human beings Providing care to underserved and vulnerable populations Ranked #1 for US medical schools having the highest percentage of students entering family medicine (30.3% in 2016-2017) Consistently ranked within the top 10 in NIH research funding among Family Medicine departments nationally and currently ranks 6 th #11 US News and World Report national ranking of top family medicine program (2023-2024) #2 US News and World Report for Most Graduates Practicing in Medically Underserved Areas (2023-2024) Approximately half of the Health Sciences Center leadership are family Physicians (most of whom are graduates of the UNM Family Medicine Residency Program) Patient Centered Care In the clinical area, the candidate will be engaged in a primary care, team-based model exploring innovative methodology of health care delivery. We have a growing number of Family Medicine clinics throughout Albuquerque in which faculty practice. These are all Patient Centered Medical Home Model and currently many of these clinics are rated the top level, PCMH (level 3). Innovative Education We are nationally and internationally known for educational innovation, currently in the area of the integration of medicine and public health. Our faculty are major contributors to the education of medical students at UNM and our residency program creates opportunities for rotations in both rural and underserved settings as well as UNM rotations. We have several Fellowships including Maternal Child Health, Sports Medicine and Rural Medicine. We boast a large number of residents practicing in New Mexico including those not native to New Mexico We are home of the UNM Physician Assistant Program About Albuquerque, New Mexico Albuquerque, NM is a beautiful city with mountains to the east and a mesa to the west. It is ideal for outdoor activities and sports all year round including running, hiking, biking and skiing. Albuquerque is 1 hour from Santa Fe, NM and 2.5 hours from Taos, NM, both world famous for their art and culture. The State of New Mexico is multicultural and diverse with 19 indigenous native pueblos, Navajo reservation and three Apache tribal lands. We have excellent local cuisine, breathtaking sunsets, multiple cultural and historic sites, lakes, rivers, deserts and mountains. Salary: Salary and rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Qualifications Minimum Requirements: • Medical Doctor or Doctor of Osteopathy • Board eligible/certified in Family Medicine by the ABFP or AOA • Family Medicine Obstetrics or MCH Fellowship training and experience with adequate volume to obtain operative obstetric privileges including cesarean sections, operative vaginal delivery, and postpartum dilation and curettage. • Eligible for medical licensure in NM • Eligible for State of New Mexico Board of Pharmacy certification and federal DEA registration • Must be eligible to work in the U.S. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience practicing surgical obstetrics beyond fellowship • Competency in repair of third- and fourth-degree perineal lacerations, manual vacuum aspiration, and postpartum bilateral tubal ligation • Patient care experience in an office or community clinic • Experience in educating students and residents • Addiction medicine board certification •A demonstrated commitment\nto cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and\nto the success of the university's mission to serve local and global\ncommunities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Please attach a Cover Letter and CV. For assistance with the application process, contact FCM-HR@salud.unm.edu For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 9/24/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37341?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 37341",
      "description": "Requisition: 37341 - Temp Parttime Faculty-Psychology - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Temp Parttime Faculty-Psychology Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37341 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/9/2026 Back to Search Temp Parttime Faculty-Psychology Posting Number req37341 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Adjunct Hiring Department Psychology Department (765A) Academic Location College of Arts & Sciences Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible Adjunct faculty may be eligible to receive certain UNM benefits in some cases. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The\nDepartment of Psychology is seeking qualified temporary, part-time faculty.\nAppointments are made on a semester-by-semester basis, with positions filled\nbased on budget availability, course enrollment, and departmental needs. Primary Responsibilities Responsibilities\ninclude, but are not limited to: Teaching and\n     facilitating undergraduate psychology courses. Preparing,\n     administering, and grading assignments, quizzes, midterm examinations, and\n     final examinations. Developing, updating,\n     and maintaining course materials and instructional content. Coordinating course\n     activities, including class schedules and examinations, as needed. Maintaining accurate\n     student records and submitting grades in accordance with University\n     policies and deadlines. Holding scheduled\n     office hours and responding to student inquiries in a timely manner. Assessing student\n     learning outcomes and participating in departmental assessment activities,\n     as appropriate. Performing other\n     instructional duties and responsibilities consistent with the position. Faculty\nare responsible for all aspects of the courses they teach, including meeting\nwith classes during assigned times, delivering course content, developing and\ngrading assignments, submitting final grades, and assessing student learning\noutcomes as outlined by the department. Teaching\nassignments are based on departmental needs and are subject to change. Appointment Information: Appointments\nare contingent upon departmental need each semester, as determined by student\nenrollment, the current course offering schedule, and instructional demand\ndriven by graduation requirements. For\nbest consideration, please apply by the following priority deadlines: Spring 2027: November 13, 2026 Summer 2027: April 15, 2027 Fall 2028: June 15, 2028 Applicants\ninterested in being considered for multiple semesters should indicate their\nsemester preferences in their cover letter. Qualifications To teach courses as described above are determined by Higher Learning Commission’s accreditation requirements for faculty, and must be met by one of these ways: 1. Master’s Degree or higher in Psychology or subfield for which you are applying; Or M aster’s degree or higher in a field other than Psychology that is related to the position for which you are applying; Or Successful completion of at least 18 graduate credit hours in an accredited program in the discipline or subfield for which you are applying (i.e. BA or BS degree for example). Preferred Qualifications: Two years professional experience in the specialization or subfield An earned doctorate from an accredited institution Successful teaching experience in a post-secondary institution Successful experience teaching courses using a variety of teaching modalities (such as Face-to-Face, Remote, and Fully Online) A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global communities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Candidates should submit a resume/ CV, a portfolio (if applying for a design studio or visualization course), a cover letter, list of a minimum of two references, examples of student work if available. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration This posting will remain active until 11/13/2026. Anyone who applies for a position under this posting will automatically be considered for openings in subsequent semesters unless they indicate in their cover letter that they are not interested in teaching in specific semesters. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
