    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37782?c=unm": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Requisition: 37782 - Post Doctoral Fellow - Loomba - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Post Doctoral Fellow - Loomba Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37782 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/31/2026 Back to Search Post Doctoral Fellow - Loomba Posting Number req37782 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Research Hiring Department Physics Astronomy Department (707A) Academic Location College of Arts & Sciences Campus Main - Albuquerque, NM Benefits Eligible Postdoctoral Fellows may be eligible to receive certain UNM benefits . See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The Department of Physics and Astronomy at the University of New Mexico (UNM) invites applications for two Postdoctoral/Research Scientist positions to contribute to a DOE-funded GENESIS research program applying artificial intelligence and machine learning across several domains of physics and astronomy. The successful candidates will develop an integrated image-processing pipeline and apply it to three distinct problems: rare-event searches in particle detectors (e.g. the Migdal effect and neutrino-less double beta decay), component separation in images of strong gravitational lenses, and transient identification in interferometric radio astronomy. The positions offer an unusual opportunity to develop methods that generalize across experimental particle physics, cosmology, and radio astronomy. The selected scientist(s) will be working with a multidisciplinary team at the University of New Mexico including Professor Dinesh Loomba (PI), Professor Francis-Yan Cyr-Racine, Professor Huaiyu Duan, Distinguished Professor Greg Taylor, and Research Associate Professor Jayce Dowell, together with Dr. Ralph Massarczyk at LANL. The applicants must demonstrate strong expertise in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and image processing. The duties of this position will be to design and develop an integrated, cross-domain image-processing pipeline based on a common AI workflow in collaboration with researchers in experimental particle physics, cosmology, and radio astronomy. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: · PhD in Physics, Astronomy or a related field by date of appointment · The applicants must demonstrate strong expertise in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and image processing Preferred Qualifications: · Prior postdoctoral or equivalent research experience is preferred as evidenced by the CV · Experience applying AI techniques for rare searches, such as for dark matter, where high efficiency signal detection and background rejection are required as evidenced by the CV · Experience working across a broad domain of data types: from 1D waveforms (e.g., time series) and 2D images (e.g., taken with CMOS cameras), to high dimension images such as those used in radio astronomy as evidenced by the CV · Experience working in a team that includes senior and junior researchers and graduate students as evidenced by the CV · Excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills as evidenced by the CV · A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the University's mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. Please upload a current CV to your application. Applicants who are appointed to a UNM faculty position are required to provide an official certification of successful completion of all degree requirements prior to their initial employment with UNM. For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by . This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37798?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 37798",
      "description": "Requisition: 37798 - Open Rank of Neurology - Adult Neurology - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open Rank of Neurology - Adult Neurology Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37798 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Open Rank of Neurology - Adult Neurology Posting Number req37798 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Clinician Educator Hiring Department Neurology Adult (490B) Academic Location School of Medicine Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary Open Rank of\nNeurology – Behavioral or Cognitive Neurologist or Neuropsychiatrist The University\nof New Mexico, School of Medicine, Neurology Department seeks a behavioral\nor cognitive neurologist to join our Memory and Aging team in an open rank,\nclinician educator track position who is dedicated to the clinical care of\nindividuals with cognitive disorders to help grow and shape an expanding\ncognitive neurology program. You will be part of a team of faculty who provide\nhigh-quality cognitive care and will join a multidisciplinary group of\nNeurology faculty within the Neurology Department, UNM’s Center for Memory and\nAging (CMA) and the New Mexico Alzheimer’s Disease Research Center (ADRC). Academic\nresponsibilities include participation in the teaching of medical students,\nresidents, and fellows and research activities of the department. The newly\nfunded New Mexico ADRC provides a highly collaborative environment at the\nforefront of dementia research, with innovative programs spanning advanced\nneuroimaging and blood-based biomarkers, vascular and inflammatory mechanisms\nof dementia, brain clearance and glymphatic physiology, and novel therapeutic\nand vaccine approaches. Particularly distinctive is the Center's commitment to\nbringing state-of-the-art dementia care and research directly to New Mexico's\nrural, Hispanic/Latino, and American Indian communities through community\npartnerships and culturally responsive care and research. As the Memory\nand Aging program and New Mexico ADRC continue to grow, the successful\ncandidate will have opportunities to shape new clinical, research, and\neducational initiatives and assume leadership roles aligned with their\ninterests and experience, including in cognitive neurology services, clinical\ntrials, ADRC programs, and fellowship education. The successful\ncandidate is expected to have excellent communications skills and the ability\nto work collaboratively in interdisciplinary teams. About The\nUniversity of New Mexico Neurology Department: The University of New\nMexico is the only academic medical center in the state that is associated with\na medical school. The Department of Neurology has 40 full-time and part-time\nfaculty and is home to well-established adult and child residencies and\nmultiple fellowship programs. UNM is a mission-driven institution that provides\naccess to high quality, comprehensive and specialty care to people across the\nstate of New Mexico. About\nAlbuquerque, New Mexico: Albuquerque is\na vibrant city nestled between the 10,000-foot Sandia Mountains to the east and\nthe high desert mesas to the west. The region enjoys more than 310 days of\nsunshine annually and experiences all four seasons. Summer temperatures rarely\nexceed 100°F, with low humidity typically in the teens. The area offers\nexceptional opportunities for year-round outdoor recreation, including running,\nhiking, biking, and skiing. Albuquerque is located just one hour from Santa Fe\nand approximately two and a half hours from Taos, both renowned for their arts,\nculture, and history. New Mexico is\nhome to a rich multicultural heritage, including 19 Pueblo communities, the\nNavajo Nation, and three Apache tribal lands. Residents enjoy outstanding local\ncuisine, breathtaking sunsets, and abundant cultural, historic, and natural\nattractions, including lakes, rivers, deserts, and mountains. Qualifications Minimum\nQualifications: MD degree or\nequivalent Board eligible\nor certified in Neurology or Psychiatry Experience and\ntraining in neurological disease in older adults, especially dementia,\nAlzheimer’s disease and related disorders (ADRDs) Eligible to\nwork in the U.S. Preferred\nQualifications: 2-3 years of\nclinical experience in neurological care Fellowship\ntraining in cognitive disorders A demonstrated\ncommitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New\nMexico and to the success of the university's mission to serve local and global\ncommunities. Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. A complete application should include a cover letter, CV, and three professional references. For assistance with the application process, contact NeuroHR@salud.unm.edu . For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 9/12/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
    },
    "https://unm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/18/home/requisition/37662?c=unm": {
      "title": "Requisition: 37662",
      "description": "Requisition: 37662 - Open Rank of Internal Medicine in Cardiology - UNM Jobs Career Site :: The University of New Mexico Sign In Create Profile English (US) Open Rank of Internal Medicine in Cardiology Albuquerque, NM, United States | req37662 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/28/2026 Back to Search Open Rank of Internal Medicine in Cardiology Posting Number req37662 Employment Type Faculty Faculty Type Clinician Educator Hiring Department IM Div of Cardiology (852C) Academic Location School of Medicine Benefits Eligible The University of New Mexico provides a comprehensive package of benefits including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance. In addition, UNM offers educational benefits through the tuition remission and dependent education programs. See the Benefits home page for more information. Position Summary The University of New Mexico, rated a Best National University by US News, seeks an Open Rank - Clinician Educator to join a welcoming academic environment. This opportunity provides 10% of time protected for research, teaching, and administrative work, with additional time possible based on your interests. Led by a respected leader focused on supporting faculty for career growth, you'll have the opportunity to develop sub-sub-specialty interests, work in a new 9-floor ICU/ED/OR tower opened October 2025, earn additional “moonlighting” income, and obtain J1 visa sponsorship. Join a supportive academic setting with a fun-loving group led by a director whose mission, after ensuring excellent patient care, is to maximize opportunities for every member of the Division. Start with up to 10% of time protected for teaching, research, and administrative work. Additional protected time is available. Develop on-the-job expertise in preventive CV health, advanced lipid therapy, hypertension, cardiomyopathies, imaging, and other niches, or earn an executive MBA Supplement income by “moonlighting” at our nearby affiliated community hospital. Work with our 13 terrific cardiology fellows, many of whom go on to sub-specialty fellowships at premiere national institutions Renew your idealism and faith in the profession of medicine by teaching medical students and mentoring internal medicine residents. Challenge yourself with administrative roles: Cardiology Division members in recent years have served as Deputy Secretary of Health for the State of New Mexico, Director of Telehealth for University Hospital, Executive Director of the University Medical Group, American College of Cardiology New Mexico chapter Governor, President of SCAI, and Executive Vice Chair of Internal Medicine, New Mexico is ranked 7th best state to practice in, due to “low physician burn-out rate”, 6 th lowest cost of living, and climate allowing year-round recreation, by Medscape’s “Best and Worst Places to Practice in 2024” survey. Albuquerque was ranked a Best Place to Live in and a Best Place to Retire by US News. It has excellent Livability Score from Area Vibes, with A scores for Amenities, Commute, Cost of Living, and Housing. Cost of living is below national average. The city has diverse heritage, historic sites, a vibrant food scene, and a local international airport. Albuquerque offers endless opportunities for year-round outdoor activities, including golfing, hiking, and skiing at multiple nearby mountain resorts. A world-famous hot-air balloon festival. Flamenco capital of the US. A mountain-top restaurant. The longest tram in the US. The famous Rio Grande River. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: a) Board certified/board eligible in Cardiovascular Disease by date of hire b) Board certification/board eligible in\nEchocardiography by date of hire c) Eligible to work in the United States. Preferred Qualifications: a) Skills in providing inpatient and outpatient care b) Experience with a broad spectrum of cardiovascular disease c) Teaching experience at all levels of training d) Training or experience in research e) A demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities Application Instructions Only applications submitted through\n\t\tthe official UNMJobs site will be accepted.  If you are viewing this job\n\t\tadvertisement on a 3rd party site, please\n\t\tvisit UNMJobs to submit an application. A complete application includes : - Cover Letter - CV (month/year format) For more information contact: James Blankenship at ( jblankenship@salud.unm.edu ). For Best Consideration For best consideration, please apply by 9/12/2026. This position will remain open until filled. The University of New Mexico is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class. HEJ Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Apply Now Share Save Job Requesting an Accommodation Women, minorities, veterans, and individuals with disabilities are encouraged\n              to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA),\n              the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of New Mexico policy, if\n              you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order\n              to apply for a position with the University of New Mexico, or if you cannot\n              use the online application system, please contact Human Resources at hrpr@unm.edu (505) 277-4777 for assistance with the application process. Other links: New Mexico Inspection of Public Records Act (IPRA) Campus Safety (Clery Act) Equal Opportunity Employer The University of New Mexico is an equal opportunity\n                employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex,\n                sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, veteran status,\n                disability, or any other protected class. We are committed to hiring and\n                retaining a diverse workforce and are dedicated to the goal of building\n                an inclusive and pluralistic faculty and staff. We are committed to teaching\n                and working in a multicultural environment. Visit the links below for more information regarding our commitment to equal opportunity: Compliance, Ethics and Equal Opportunity at the University of New Mexico Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal © The University of New Mexico Albuquerque, NM 87131, (505) 277-0111 New Mexico's Flagship University UNM on Facebook UNM on Instagram UNM on Twitter UNM on Tumblr UNM on YouTube more at social.unm.edu Website Comments Accessibility Legal Select one: I am a current UNM Student I have never worked at UNM I am a current UNM Faculty or Staff, or a Retiree I am a former UNM Faculty or Staff Close Continue dataLayer = [{'site-analytics': 'UA-12990591-5'}]; (function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src='//www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-WQT2MB');"
